<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ivailo</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1280</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Ivaylo</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ivailo was a swineherd who led a peasant rebellion in north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgaria">Bulgaria</a> in 1277 against Mongol raids and the failures of the nobility. He defeated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongols">Mongols</a>, killed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tsar">Tsar</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantine-tikh">Constantine Tikh</a> in battle and was recognised as tsar, ruling until 1280. Besieged by the Mongols and abandoned by the boyars, he fled to the Mongol leader Nogai, who had him killed.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ivailo.jpg" alt="Ivailo" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Красимир Косев · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:6570_Ivaylovgrad,_Bulgaria_-_panoramio_(5).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
